@baseUrl = https://localhost:7226
@currentPassword = <supply-locally-do-not-commit>
@newPassword = <supply-locally-do-not-commit>
@authenticatedCsrf = <fresh-authenticated-token>
@csrfToken = <fresh-token-for-current-session>

### Fetch a CSRF request token; keep the antiforgery cookie in the same client session.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/account/csrf

### Login requires the token from the response above in X-CSRF-TOKEN and its cookie.
### Supply your own confirmed, trusted-provisioned account and password locally; do not commit credentials.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: <token-from-csrf-response>

{
  "gymId": 1,
  "email": "member@example.com",
  "password": "<local-password>"
}

### Send the identity cookie obtained at login in the same client session.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/account/me

### Refresh CSRF after login; use the authenticated token below, not the pre-login token.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/account/csrf

### Logout only this client: send both cookies and the authenticated CSRF token, with no body.
### Expected: empty 204, no-store, expired application cookie. Other sessions remain valid.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/logout
X-CSRF-TOKEN: <authenticated-token-from-csrf-response>

### Expected: 401 after this client processes the logout Set-Cookie response.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/account/me

### Before another login, fetch a fresh anonymous CSRF token; refresh again after login.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/account/csrf

### Alternative to logout: change your own password while still authenticated.
### Fetch authenticated CSRF first. No account, gym, or role selector belongs in this body.
### Expected: empty 204/no-store, current cookie expired; ALL old sessions/copies rejected on next request.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{authenticatedCsrf}}

{
  "currentPassword": "{{currentPassword}}",
  "newPassword": "{{newPassword}}"
}

### After success: fresh anonymous CSRF, explicit login with the NEW password and original gym selector,
### then fresh authenticated CSRF. Never log or commit real passwords or tokens.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/account/csrf
### Anonymous recovery: fetch a fresh CSRF token using the same cookie jar first.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "email": "member@example.invalid",
  "gymId": 2
}

### Future frontend obtains the opaque token only from the emailed fragment, never from an API preview.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "token": "<protected-token-from-email-fragment>",
  "newPassword": "<privately-chosen-password>"
}
